  {
    "episode_id": 42598,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42598.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Well, mostly what I've been doing is staying home, like most of you. But I have been making some face masks, too. And I've had kind of fun. As we walked in, you saw our face masks that we wore. I made that one. And last night, I decided, since I was doing more cooking than usual, that I had to make an apron to match it. So I have an apron to match my face mask. So that's my fashion statement for today. And I thought what would be good is, you know, because we're trying to teach our children to be safe as well. I made face masks for all my little grandkids. And some of them are even little tad who's just a year and a half. I made this little tiny one for him with some elastic on the back. So anyway, that's, that's Tad's. I put up a couple of recipes, one for kids. I put up my recipe for sidewalk chalk paint. I know a lot of people have been doing beautiful work with sidewalk chalk, and it's hard to find it, and you don't want to go to the store and look for it. And so my recipe just uses cornstarch and water. It's a cup of cornstarch, a cup of water, and either kids paint with it or food coloring. and you can go out and paint the sidewalk. It's a great thing for kids to do outside. I'm also putting up my grandmother's whole wheat bread recipe. I usually don't make it because it takes a long time to make it, but since I'm home, it works out pretty well. And it uses a lot less yeast than normal bread because you put half the flour in, let it rise for a while and that yeast grows, and then you put the other half in. So those are just a couple of the things that I'm doing at home. I made some face masks for friends. One friend said, if I made him five, he would give $500 to my favorite charity. So I said, if you'll give it to a food bank, I'll do it. So, you know, I just think we really need to help these food banks and send them money because they really are feeding a lot of people today. Thank you.",
