    "turn_text": "Thank you very much, Governor. Some good news on this good Friday that I wanted to share. Early this morning, I got a call from folks at Stairus, which is a company up in Menor, Ohio. And they let me know that they received FDA approval for small scale N95 mask decontamination. So we know the large scale things that Battelle is doing for us in Ohio, Stairus received small scale approval to do this. It's through their VPRO, which is a vaporizing hydrogen peroxide sterilizer, easy for me to say. That's the technology that they use. Battelle can do up to 80,000 a day per machine, but these are smaller scale, smaller that can fit into a business healthcare facility. They do 10 masks in 28 minutes, and they have 100 of these machines across Ohio. So it's just another example of the Ohio innovators out there, the businesses who are stepping up and solving problems. The technology for this was was developed right there in Menor, Ohio at the Stairus facility and we thank our innovators and entrepreneurs and healthcare professionals who are really just solving problems every day out there and it's fantastic news. Additionally, I wanted to say you probably, if any of you have school-age children like Tina and I do, our children are at home conducting school every day. Our daughters do it online. And it's worked out great, but yesterday I came home and my daughter Katie had shown me a mask that she made for me. She went in my drawer and tore out some old t-shirts and just folded them over and made them. They did this as part of their seventh grade life skills class that Pam Meadows, their teacher, conducted for them, and these work great. So you can, everybody has an old t-shirt laying around the house, and while they're not as quite as fancy as the one that the first lady has been",
