    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Thank you so much. So we know that a vaccine is at least a year to a year and a half away. And so this is not a journey that ends just in this immediate future. We will still have large parts of our population that have not yet been exposed. That is why we absolutely need to scale up our testing capability in this country. without that valuable tool, it really makes it a lot harder for us to be able to tell, first of all, if someone's had it and recovered, but it also is how we will be able to, once we're stabilized, our hospitals are built up, we have the PPE we need to handle the emergency responses, we have the PPE in our nursing homes, in our prisons, for our frontline responders in our EMS. When we have all of those things, then when we have a test and we see it'll go back to the sort of beginning of this, our usual epidemiologic work, we will be able to catch a case right away and then contact all the people who've been exposed to them and that select group can quarantine. And we'll be able to be sure that the others have not been exposed. So we really need those tools to truly start to move out of the woods. Thank you.",
