    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "Adrian Robbins, NBC4, and my questions for either the governor or the lieutenant governor. We hear about these companies quickly getting FDA approval and how we're cutting through red tape to allow our companies to be innovative. Do you think when this is all over we'll look back and realize a lot of the red tape that we put companies through probably isn't necessary? Or right now are we just taking the necessary risk to cut that red tape?",
