  {
    "episode_id": 42598,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42598.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 71,
    "turn_text": "You know, some of them were just invented and approved by the FDA, again, through the emergency youth authorization that the lieutenant governor said. And so the companies are rapidly trying to develop them and then get them on board. And that just that the scaling up in production is slow for some of the other testing. They're a complicated set of reagents that have a global supply chain to those. They're proprietary in nature as well. So it's a complicated, complicated set of situations that has occurred and again greatly impacted by the fact that this is a global pandemic. Lieutenant Governor.",
