  {
    "episode_id": 42598,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42598.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "When I started making calls to these companies earlier in the week, there was only, I think as of last Sunday, there was only one that I'm aware of in the country that had been approved. Some of the other countries that were doing, but there was only one in America that had been approved for this, and we were one of the first calls that they had. We're supposed to get a thousand of those really soon. I don't know when that's going to be, but we're hopefully get those soon. But when I talk with one of the companies and ask them what we could expect in terms of timing on this, what they said is they said, look, our experience around the globe is this, that once you develop a test, everybody wants you to go fast and produce it. But you have to make sure that that test has a reliability that you need because what you don't want to do is start and get out there and have a test that only works 70 or 80% of the time, then you will have wasted your time. And so that's why it's a little slow in developing because they need to validate it so that you can make sure that what you have has the reliability that you need to make sure that your efforts are actually have value. And so that's happening very fast. I think that that feedback that I've had is that we are weeks away from this. I think when you get to May, that's when it's gonna really, we really hope to have more of these on hand.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_17",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
