  {
    "episode_id": 42598,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42598.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 75,
    "turn_text": "Sure, without knowing the specifics of their situation, it's a really difficult question to answer. Because those questions come to me, and what do I do? I pose those same questions to the people who are running the system in Director Hall. And believe me, even as this news conference has gone on, I have been on the phone texting her and saying, you know, what guidance do you have on some of these things? The feedback that I've received has been that for everybody who's been who's applied and has been approved, that we're caught up. That's going out. But there are occasions when somebody may be contacting the folks at unemployment and they don't have all the information they need to actually apply. And I know that can be frustrating. So that's why I would encourage folks before you try to get through, go to the website and read everything that you're going to need to be able to provide them. Again, And this system was not designed for these circumstances. The system is usually designed for checks and balances to make sure that somebody doesn't try to take something from the system that they haven't earned. And so that's why those safeguards are put in place. But in a time like this, the safeguards can seem frustrating because you, it's like I have to have this and I have to have that. So go to the website, make sure you get all the information that you know you're going to need to apply, have that in place first, and then know that They're supposed to get back to you as quickly as they can if you have not, if you don't have what you need so that they can help you get through that process. But it's very difficult to answer that specific question because they don't know what to hold up. We also know that there are some people who are applying, who are not eligible, all of those kinds of things. can lead to the frustration, and so I'm empathetic to what folks are going through. Every day we build more capacity, we build more problem solving solutions into it, and I just ask that you are patient as we're building this out. I know that if you are in desperate need of those resources, that asking to be patient is not good enough, but believe me, everything that I get from you, I'm taking to them and asking them to solve these problems. Thank you.",
