  {
    "episode_id": 42598,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/2/42598.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 100,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, they're training the capacity that the system, I mean, they're putting people on, we have, I think, 20 times, I don't want to, I think it's, we're up to 1,000 people now who are working, they're working on everything from the phones to processing claims, adding people all the time, someone has to be trained to be able to do this. There's a process for following the federal and state laws to do this, and we've ramped up faster than I actually thought we even could. So that is happening. As far as processing claims, that has caught up. They are catching up on On the capacity for the calling system, it will be open. I don't know what the hours are over the Easter weekend, but they've been operating every weekend, including Saturdays and Sundays, and the online system is available 24 hours a day. Every single day, they're building more and more of that capacity. As I've said on several times today already, I am very empathetic to what's going on. Everything that I hear from you, everything that I hear from them is getting driven down into the system so that they know that they have to respond. I can tell you everybody who works at unemployment compensation gets the urgency of this. This is not like they're unaware of it, and they're building out that capacity as fast as they can. But I do want to put this in perspective that when you see the unemployment numbers, there are more people that are applying for unemployment in three weeks than we typically have in years. It is, I guess, in a month. We're having more in a month than we would see over the course of years. And the system just wasn't built for that. And so we're trying to build a system while serving people all at the same time.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_17",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "There are currently around 1,000 people working on the unemployment system.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The online system is accessible 24/7 every day.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "A formal process exists for complying with federal and state laws related to unemployment claims.",
